FOUNDER
- Yang Chia Shan (also known as "Captain Yang" or "Elder Yang"): born December 2, 1924 in Beijing, China; graduate of the National Merchant Marine Academy in Guangzhou; became the youngest captain in the history of Taiwan Shipping Company; later became a philanthropist and Christian educational leader; co-founded IUCA through his organizations CASA (Central Asia Sharing Aid) and the Yrayym Foundation; funded the university's construction and scholarship programs to support underprivileged students

ACCREDITATION
- All academic programs of IUCA and HTC regularly undergo accreditation by the EdNet agency
- EdNet is a full member of the Asia-Pacific Quality Network (APQN) and the European Association for Quality Assurance in Higher Education (ENQA)
- In 2025, EdNet became the first and only international member of the Council for Higher Education Accreditation (CHEA, USA), giving IUCA diplomas international status
- Current accreditation certificates: EdNet general 2024–2029; 5 programs 2024–2026; Business Administration; Law; Information Technologies

BACHELOR'S PROGRAMS (7 programs)
1. Business Administration
   - Mission: Shape professional leaders and managers capable of managing business processes in a dynamic economic environment
   - Focus: Strategic thinking, marketing, leadership, entrepreneurial skills, critical thinking, ethical values
   - Business Clinic: Active since September 2016; provides advisory and consulting services to local entrepreneurs, run by senior students under faculty guidance

2. Information Technology
   - Mission: Comprehensive and quality training of qualified software development specialists at the bachelor's level
   - Focus: Software development, databases, algorithms, web technologies, graphics, audio/video applications

3. International Relations
   - Profile: Prevention of Regional Conflicts
   - Mission: Train modern, competitive, multilingual specialists in international relations with high social activity and responsibility
   - Focus: Diplomacy, international politics, conflict management, conflictology, negotiation skills, international dialogue

4. Law
   - Mission: Train a new generation of professionals for domestic and international legal markets through close integration of education, science, and practice
   - Focus: National and international law, business law, legal document drafting, analytical and communication skills
   - Legal Clinic: Provides free legal consultations to Tokmok community members, run by senior law students under supervision of qualified faculty lawyers

5. Linguistics. English Language
   - Mission: Form highly qualified professionals capable of effective teaching and intercultural communication with critical thinking and continuous self-improvement
   - Focus: Fundamental linguistics, excellent English, second foreign language (German or French), teaching methodology, translation
   - Classes conducted in English; teachers hold international certificates (TESOL, British Council, DAAD)

6. Linguistics. Chinese Language
   - Mission: Train competent professionals with intercultural communication skills and command of Chinese; critical thinking, global mindset
   - Focus: Chinese language interpretation, Chinese culture, intercultural communication; interpreters described as "a bridge linking two peoples"

7. Pedagogy
   - Mission: Prepare qualified educators capable of implementing innovative teaching methods, fostering creative thinking, and developing leadership skills in education
   - Focus: Theoretical knowledge, practical teaching skills, ethical principles for careers in education

MASTER'S PROGRAM (1 program)
- MA Program in Pedagogy
  - Developed in partnership with the "Zamanap Mugalim — Teach for Kyrgyzstan" Foundation, a member of the international Teach for All network
  - Dual education principle: students simultaneously work as teachers in public schools and study, immediately applying knowledge in practice
  - Mission: Prepare a new generation of teacher-leaders capable of transforming education in rural schools of Kyrgyzstan
  - Selection: Every year, the "Zamanap Mugalim" Foundation selects young professionals committed to contributing to education

