SCHOLARSHIPS AND FINANCIAL AID
- Full Scholarship (100% tuition): Awarded to students scoring 200 or above on the ORT main test. IUCA provides 12 full scholarships. Criteria also include TOEFL PBT score over 450.
- Trustee Scholarships: Provided by university trustees; can cover 100% of tuition, guest house fees, and personal expenses; awarded based on financial status and academic performance
- Partial Financial Aid (20%–75% of tuition): Available for students from low-income, large, or single-parent families; orphans; students with excellent academic progress (GPA 3.5+)
- Merit Discounts: Awarded to top-performing students at end of each academic year
- Documents required for financial aid application: family composition certificate; State Register property documents for all adult family members; property market value certificate; vehicle ownership documents; income statements for all adult family members; additional documents for unemployed, private entrepreneur, retiree, or disabled family members; utility bills for the last 6 months (heating, electricity, gas); enrollment certificate for other university-attending family members

ADMISSIONS — KYRGYZ CITIZENS
- Application: In person (Mon–Fri, 9:00–16:00) or online at https://admission.iuca.kg
- Minimum ORT score: 110
- Required documents:
  1. Application form
  2. 6 photos 3x4 cm (color, matte) + 1 digital photo
  3. Copy of passport
  4. Original ORT certificate (minimum score 110)
  5. Original school graduation diploma (Attestat)
  6. Certificate of enlistment or military ID (for conscripts only)

ADMISSIONS — FOREIGN / INTERNATIONAL CITIZENS
- Application: In person (Mon–Fri, 9:00–16:00) or online at https://admission.iuca.kg
- Requirement: Pass the university's internal English and general knowledge exams
- Required documents:
  1. Application form
  2. Copy of passport
  3. High school diploma (original)
  4. 6 photos 3x4 cm
  5. Medical documents: vaccination record (including COVID-19); information on chronic diseases; HIV and syphilis test results (two weeks before visa application); chest X-ray with medical record (two weeks before visa application)
  6. Certificate of enlistment or military ID (for CIS citizens on military register, to obtain service deferment)

VISA AND REGISTRATION GUIDE FOR INTERNATIONAL STUDENTS
- Step 1: Check visa requirements at https://www.evisa.e-gov.kg (Ministry of Foreign Affairs of KR)
- Step 2: Apply for initial student visa ("Applicant" category) — the International Office prepares the official support letter
  - Processing time: 7–10 working days
  - Validity: 1–3 months
  - Single entry cost: 4,500–5,500 KGS (52–62 USD)
  - Multiple entry cost: 5,500–7,300 KGS (62–83 USD)
  - Urgent processing (2 working days): 16,500–22,000 KGS (185–248 USD)
- Step 3: Registration at place of temporary stay via TsON (Public Service Center), Ibraimova Street 1/1, Tokmok; fee: 632 KGS; requires passport, study contract, IUCA support letter, visa copy, and property owner's presence
  - Dormitory residents register via International Office (Building A, 3rd floor, Room 308); fee: 641 KGS; processed online via EREG system within 1 working day
- Step 4: One-year student visa — must be prepared 20 days before initial visa expires; requires Mandatory Health Insurance Policy (OMS)
  - Multiple entry cost: 15,400 KGS (176 USD)
  - Single entry cost: 9,500 KGS (109 USD)
  - Urgent processing: 30,000–46,000 KGS (325–525 USD)
- Step 5: Annual registration — same procedure as initial registration
- International Affairs Office contact: iao@iuca.kg; Building A, 3rd floor, Room 308

